      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2000 European Paediatric Neurology Society.",
        "AbstractText": "A child with macrocephaly-cutis marmorata developed severe abdominal pain thought to represent mesenteric angina. There were abnormalities of the aortic and mesenteric vasculature not previously reported in this condition. Angina therapy afforded amelioration of his symptoms. Mesenteric angina should be considered as a cause for abdominal pain in children with mesodermal anomalies."
      },
